  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A coastal low will impact at least Downeast \nMaine late this week bringing gusty winds, high surf, and rain.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION... \nA coastal low is expected to develop across the Mid-Atlantic \nregion late this week while high pressure remains centered over \nQuebec. The timing and track of the ocean low is still uncertain\nwith blocking high pressure to the northwest of our forecast \narea and ridging across the Great Lakes. Latest guidance has the\nrain entering the area during the early part of the weekend. \nThere is still uncertainty of how close the low pressure will \npass to the coast which will determine the amount of precip that\nreaches inland. Regardless, northerly to northeasterly winds \nwill become gusty over the weekend, especially along the coast, \nas a tight pressure gradient forms. General trend currently is \nthat the low pressure system will continue to stay south of the \nregion due to the high pressure, with majority of the rain \nstaying over the waters and the Downeast region. &&",
